ation-symbol scheme="EC">C07C  51/09+57/10</classification-symbol></classification-ecla><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="EN">PROCESS FOR THE PREPARATION OF SORBIC ACID</invention-title><invention-title load-source="docdb"  status="new" lang="FR">PROCEDE DE PREPARATION D'ACIDE SORBIQUE</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-44026646-B1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>44026646</doc-number><kind>B1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-54103821-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>54103821</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1035097A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data> <parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DAICEL CHEM</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONO MITSUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAICEL CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUNO, MITSUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOUNO MITSUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUNO, MITSUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for the preparation of sorbic acid by subjecting a polyester prepared from ketene and crotonaldehyde to decomposition with hydrochloric acid at 100  DEG C or below, wherein the reaction temperature after the initiation of decomposition of the polyester is controlled by adding to the reaction fluid hydrochloric acid whose temperature is lower than that of the reaction fluid, e.g., 50  DEG C or below. The hydrochloric acid to be used in the reaction control may have a concentration of, e.g., 23 wt. % or above. This process can give sorbic acid in a shortened time and in an enhanced yield, thus attaining a high production efficiency.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de préparation d'acide sorbique consistant à soumettre un polyester préparé à partir de cétène et de crotonaldéhyde à une décomposition avec de l'acide chlorhydrique à 100  DEG C ou moins, dans lequel la température de réaction après le début de la décomposition du polyester est régulée par addition au fluide de réaction d'acide chlorhydrique dont la température est inférieure à celle du fluide de réaction, par exemple, de 50  DEG C ou moins. L'acide chlorhydrique à utiliser dans la régulation de la réaction peut avoir une concentration, par exemple, de 23 % en poids ou davantage. Ce procédé peut donner de l'acide sorbique en un temps raccourci et à un rendement supérieur, atteignant ainsi une productivité élevée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>